collections:
  - folderType: environment
    id: 766dd6c4-001c-4000-8000-766dd6c4766d
    name: Swagger Petstore
    documentation: |-
      # Swagger Petstore

      This is a sample server Petstore server.  You can find out more about Swagger at [http://swagger.io](http://swagger.io) or on [irc.freenode.net, #swagger](http://swagger.io/irc/).  For this sample, you can use the api key &#x60;special-key&#x60; to test the authorization filters.

      **Version:** 1.0.7

      **Terms of Service:** [http://swagger.io/terms/](http://swagger.io/terms/)

      ## Contact

      - **Email:** [apiteam@swagger.io](mailto:apiteam@swagger.io)

      ## License

      [Apache 2.0](http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.html)

      ## External Documentation

      [Find out more about Swagger](http://swagger.io)

      **Host:** `localhost:8080`

      **Base Path:** `/api`

      **Schemes:** `https`, `http`

      ## Models

      ```mermaid
      classDiagram
        class Category {
          - id? : integer
          - name? : string
        }
        class Pet {
          - id? : integer
          - category? : Category
          + name : string
          + photoUrls : array<string>
          - tags? : array<Tag>
          - status? : string
        }
        class Tag {
          - id? : integer
          - name? : string
        }
        class ApiResponse {
          - code? : integer
          - type? : string
          - message? : string
        }
        class Order {
          - id? : integer
          - petId? : integer
          - quantity? : integer
          - shipDate? : string
          - status? : string
          - complete? : boolean
        }
        class User {
          - id? : integer
          - username? : string
          - firstName? : string
          - lastName? : string
          - email? : string
          - password? : string
          - phone? : string
          - userStatus? : integer
        }
        Pet --> Category
        Pet --> Tag
      ```
    tags: []
    configuration: {}
    environments:
      - id: 202eb0f6-0010-4000-8000-202eb0f6202e
        name: Default
        variables:
          - key: baseUrl
            value: http://localhost:8080
            description: ''
        subEnvironments:
          - id: 47687a23-001b-4000-8000-47687a234768
            name: Production
            variables:
              - key: baseUrl
                value: https://petstore.com
    items:
      - id: 658d6a33-000e-4000-8000-658d6a33658d
        name: pet
        documentation: "# pet\r\n\r\nEverything about your Pets\r\n\r\n## External Documentation\r\n\r\n[Find out more](http://swagger.io)"
        tags:
          - pet
        configuration: {}
        items:
          - type: http
            id: 48e1f7f2-0018-4000-8000-48e1f7f248e1
            name: Find pet by ID
            documentation: |-
              # Find pet by ID

              Returns a single pet

              **Operation ID:** `getPetById`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `petId` | path | integer (int64) | Yes | ID of pet to return |

              ## Types

              ### Pet

              **Reference:** `#/definitions/Pet`

              ```mermaid
              classDiagram
                class Pet {
                  - id? : integer
                  - category? : Category
                  + name : string
                  + photoUrls : array<string>
                  - tags? : array<Tag>
                  - status? : string
                }
              ```


              | Property | Type | Required | Description |
              |----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `id` | integer | No |  |
              | `category` | Category | No |  |
              | `name` | string | Yes |  |
              | `photoUrls` | array&lt;string&gt; | Yes |  |
              | `tags` | array&lt;Tag&gt; | No |  |
              | `status` | string | No | pet status in the store |


              ## Responses

              ### 200
              successful operation

              **Schema:** `#/definitions/Pet`


              ### 400
              Invalid ID supplied



              ### 404
              Pet not found



              ## Security

              - **api_key**
            tags:
              - pet
            method: GET
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/pet/{{petId}}'
            headers: []
            params: []
            pathParams:
              - key: petId
                value: ''
                description: ID of pet to return
          - type: http
            id: 7d41454e-0019-4000-8000-7d41454e7d41
            name: Updates a pet in the store with form data
            documentation: |-
              # Updates a pet in the store with form data

              **Operation ID:** `updatePetWithForm`

              ## Consumes

              - `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `petId` | path | integer (int64) | Yes | ID of pet that needs to be updated |
              | `name` | formData | string | No | Updated name of the pet |
              | `status` | formData | string | No | Updated status of the pet |

              ## Responses

              ### 405
              Invalid input



              ## Security

              - **petstore_auth**: `write:pets`, `read:pets`
            tags:
              - pet
            method: POST
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/pet/{{petId}}'
            headers: []
            params: []
            pathParams:
              - key: petId
                value: ''
                description: ID of pet that needs to be updated
            body:
              type: x-www-form-urlencoded
              fields:
                - key: name
                  value: ''
                  description: Updated name of the pet
                - key: status
                  value: ''
                  description: Updated status of the pet
          - type: http
            id: 2e127f1d-001b-4000-8000-2e127f1d2e12
            name: Deletes a pet
            documentation: |-
              # Deletes a pet

              **Operation ID:** `deletePet`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`
              - `application/xml`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `api_key` | header | string | No |  |
              | `petId` | path | integer (int64) | Yes | Pet id to delete |

              ## Responses

              ### 400
              Invalid ID supplied



              ### 404
              Pet not found



              ## Security

              - **petstore_auth**: `write:pets`, `read:pets`
            tags:
              - pet
            method: DELETE
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/pet/{{petId}}'
            headers:
              - key: api_key
                value: ''
            params: []
            pathParams:
              - key: petId
                value: ''
                description: Pet id to delete
          - type: http
            id: 484c6099-0025-4000-8000-484c6099484c
            name: uploads an image
            documentation: |-
              # uploads an image

              **Operation ID:** `uploadFile`

              ## Consumes

              - `multipart/form-data`

              ## Produces

              - `application/json`

              ## Parameters

              | Name | Location | Type | Required | Description |
              |------|----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `petId` | path | integer (int64) | Yes | ID of pet to update |
              | `additionalMetadata` | formData | string | No | Additional data to pass to server |
              | `file` | formData | file | No | file to upload |

              ## Types

              ### ApiResponse

              **Reference:** `#/definitions/ApiResponse`

              ```mermaid
              classDiagram
                class ApiResponse {
                  - code? : integer
                  - type? : string
                  - message? : string
                }
              ```


              | Property | Type | Required | Description |
              |----------|------|----------|-------------|
              | `code` | integer | No |  |
              | `type` | string | No |  |
              | `message` | string | No |  |


              ## Responses

              ### 200
              successful operation

              **Schema:** `#/definitions/ApiResponse`


              ## Security

              - **petstore_auth**: `write:pets`, `read:pets`
            tags:
              - pet
            method: POST
            url: '{{baseUrl}}/api/pet/{{petId}}/uploadImage'
            headers: []
            params: []
            pathParams:
              - key: petId
                value: ''
                description: ID of pet to update
            body:
              type: form-data
              fields:
                - key: additionalMetadata
                  value: ''
                  description: Additional data to pass to server
                - key: file
                  value: ''
                  description: file to upload
          - type: http
            id: 5d99e601-0011-4000-8000-5d99e6015d99
            name: Add a new pet to the store
            documentation: |-
